```

My concern is that now the type is generic, yet the constructor still takes an `object?` (not a `T?`), and the target is still also just an `object?`. We can't make those be `T?`, because in the array case you'd be passing a `T[]` object instead. So basically the only advantage of this being generic is that we can have the slightly faster `GetSZArrayDataPointer` variant, and we can have those two returning `T*` (which is nice, sure), but on the other hand we now have a type that is generic and still doesn't use that generic type argument at all in most cases (in fact, it will let you do weird things like using the wrong type argument entirely, and it'll still work just fine in the non-array case). And the type being generic while still just having those `object?` params feels awkward 🤔

Am I missing something here and is there some way to work around this that I'm not seeing?
Because if not, I think maybe the non-generic version with no SZ array helper makes more sense after all.

